Windows packaged-acceptance diagnosis after repeated failures.

Observed evidence:
- Diagnostic run 33975097548 failed twice after a real standard extension reached register, then activate.
- Both attempts persisted extensions_stop_unconfirmed, while the changing last load stage proved the process had crossed the Node handshake and entered host.load.
- The runtime reused a stop deadline created before fingerprinting, host startup, handshake, and requests that may each wait up to 30 seconds. A subsequent cleanup therefore received an already-expired 5-second deadline and overwrote the original load failure with a misleading stop failure.

Correction:
- Stop deadlines are now created at the exact process-stop boundary, independently for stale channels, rejected spawns, failed loads, tool-call invalidation, and post-sync lookup.
- Restart keeps the user-owned stop deadline only for the old generation; starting the new generation is a separate phase.
- Windows private ACL application and verification reuse the single existing 2-second bounded filesystem retry authority. Every attempt reapplies and re-verifies the exact ACL, and permanent failure remains fail-closed.
- The isolated Windows private-store harness now performs 128 atomic replacements, and the fast windows-host CI target executes it before any packaged CEF rebuild.

